This photo shows a tray after a meal, with almost no food left. Visible leftovers are a few green smears (probably peas or a sauce) on the large plate, light crumbs on the small plates, a little yogurt in the cup, a pink residue in the small bowl, and some coffee or tea stains in the mug.

The remaining food is only traces. I estimate about 15 g in total: yogurt about 8 g, residue on the plates about 5 g, and a little in the bowl. At roughly 1 kcal/g, that comes to about 15 kcal.

